          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Finding the Unknown"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.089,
            0.847,
            0.148
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "of the names of colours — kālaka (black), nīlaka (blue), and so on. In contrast to these unknowns, the known quantities in an expression had a specific form (rūpa) and were denoted by rū."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.148,
            0.847,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here are some examples of how algebraic expressions in modern "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "notation were written in ancient Indian notation:",
              "styles": [
                "underline"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.193,
            0.842,
            0.465
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.155,
                0.193,
                0.842,
                0.465
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_19_table_3.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Modern Notation</td><td>Ancient Indian Notation</td></tr><tr><td>2x + 1</td><td>yā 2 rū 1 (in each term the indication of unknown/known came first)</td></tr><tr><td>2x - 8</td><td>yā 2 rū8. (a dot over the number indicated that it was negative)</td></tr><tr><td>3x + 4 = 2x + 8</td><td>yā 3 rū 4 yā 2 rū 8 (the two sides of an equation were presented one below the other)</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.487,
            0.846,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 16: Bījgaṇita by Bhāskarāchārya (1150 CE) mentions this problem."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.533,
            0.847,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "One man has ₹300 rupees and 6 horses. Another man has 10 horses and a debt of ₹100. If they are equally rich and the price of each horse is the same, tell me the price of one horse."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.598,
            0.253,
            0.616
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution:"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.622,
            0.42,
            0.642
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let price of one horse = ₹ x"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.646,
            0.406,
            0.667
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "According to the problem"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.383,
            0.674,
            0.583,
            0.695
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_19_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "300+6x=10x-100"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.385,
            0.703,
            0.598,
            0.724
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_19_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "300+6x+(100)=10x"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.385,
            0.732,
            0.529,
            0.751
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_19_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "400+6x=10x"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.385,
            0.76,
            0.528,
            0.779
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_19_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "400 = 10x - 6x"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.385,
            0.788,
            0.475,
            0.808
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_19_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "4 0 0 = 4 x"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.385,
            0.817,
            0.496,
            0.837
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_19_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "400 \\div 4 = x"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.385,
            0.845,
            0.463,
            0.865
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_19_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "1 0 0 = x"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.87,
            0.552,
            0.89
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, the price of one horse = ₹ 100."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
